13. Synchronous and Asynchronous Programming Using Node.js
File: async.js
const fs = require("fs");

console.log("Program Started");

// Synchronous
let data = fs.readFileSync("student.txt", "utf8");
console.log("Sync:", data);

// Asynchronous
fs.readFile("student.txt", "utf8", (err, data) => {
    if (err) {
        console.log(err);
    } else {
        console.log("Async:", data);
    }
});

console.log("Program Ended");


Run:
node async.js


Expected concept:
- Synchronous: Executes line by line and waits for completion.
- Asynchronous: Does not wait; continues executing other statements.
- Callback: A function passed as an argument to another function.
- Event Loop: Handles asynchronous callbacks when the call stack is free.

